---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const title = `Terms of Service - ${site.name}`;
const description =
  'The terms that govern your use of Stock4, the stock-control service operated by iCentric Systems Ltd.';

// Bump this whenever the wording below is materially changed.
const effectiveDate = '16 July 2026';
const contactEmail = site.email;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-5 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <header class="mb-8">
        <h1 class="display text-3xl md:text-4xl text-brand-950 m-0">Terms of Service</h1>
        <p class="text-sm text-ink-500 mt-3 m-0">Effective {effectiveDate}</p>
      </header>

      <div class="flex flex-col gap-10 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">1. Acceptance</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            By creating an account or using Stock4 (the “Service”), you agree to these Terms of
            Service (“Terms”). If you do not agree, do not use the Service. The Service is provided
            by {site.company}, trading as {site.studio} (“we”, “us”, “Stock4”).
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">2. Your account</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            Stock4 accounts are held by a company, which may invite users and assign them access
            roles. You are responsible for keeping your credentials safe and for activity under your
            account, and your company is responsible for managing its users’ access. Let us know
            promptly if you suspect unauthorised access. You must be at least 18 years old to use the
            Service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">3. Subscription &amp; billing</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            The Service is offered on a one-off setup fee plus a monthly subscription and a per-user
            charge, across the tiers shown on our pricing page. Paid subscriptions are billed monthly
            via our payment processor, Stripe, until cancelled. Indicative pricing shown before or at
            sign-up may change; we will give existing subscribers at least 30 days’ notice of any
            price change.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Cancellations take effect at the end of the current billing period. We don’t refund
            unused portions of a paid period except where required by law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">4. Acceptable use</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            Don’t use Stock4 to break the law, infringe others’ rights, store content you don’t have
            the right to store, or interfere with the operation of the Service (including by reverse
            engineering, scraping at unreasonable volumes, or attempting to bypass billing). We may
            suspend or terminate accounts that do.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">5. Your content &amp; data</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            You retain ownership of everything you put into Stock4 - stock items, stock takes,
            orders, suppliers, pricing and related records. You grant us the permissions needed to
            store and display it back to you and the users you invite into your account. See our
            <a href="/privacy/" class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>
            for how we handle personal data.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">6. Intellectual property</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            The Stock4 software, brands (including the Glazing, Building, Plumbing and Electrics trade
            apps), design and documentation are owned by {site.company} and protected by copyright
            and trademark law. These Terms don’t transfer any of that to you; they only let you use
            the Service.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">7. Liability</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            The Service is provided “as is”. To the extent permitted by law, we exclude implied
            warranties, and our total liability for any claim arising from the Service is limited to
            the amount you paid us in the 12 months before the claim arose. Nothing in these Terms
            limits liability for death, personal injury or fraud.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Stock4 is a stock-management tool. While we work to keep it accurate, we make no warranty
            that stock levels, pricing or ordering figures generated by the Service are correct for
            any specific purpose - verify critical figures before acting on them.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">8. Termination</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            You may cancel and close your account at any time by contacting us; doing so wipes your
            data on our side except where retention is required by law (e.g. tax records). We may
            terminate or suspend access for breach of these Terms or where we are required to do so
            by law.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">9. Changes to these Terms</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            We may update these Terms occasionally. Material changes will be flagged in-app or by
            email; the “Effective” date at the top of this page tracks the current version.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-ink-900 m-0">10. Governing law &amp; contact</h2>
          <p class="m-0">
            These Terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales, and the courts of England and
            Wales have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Questions about these Terms?
            <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-brand-700 hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
